    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Gemma3RMSNorm.forward_cuda` fuses only 2D input. q_norm and k_norm get `[tokens, heads, head_dim]` and fall back to the eager chain, 10 kernels per norm. This is the 3D follow-up hnyls2002 suggested on #21962.\n\n## Modifications\n\nHigher-rank input is flattened for `gemma_rmsnorm`, as `Gemma4RMSNorm` does. The gemma3_mm vision embedding norm also takes this path. The new test fails on `main`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\ngemma-3-4b-it, GSM8K 400 questions, RTX 3090: main 0.750, this PR 0.740 (standard error about 2.2 points), invalid 0.000 on both. The fused output matches `forward_native` to one bf16 step.\n\n```\npython -m sglang.test.few_shot_gsm8k --num-questions 400 --parallel 64\n```\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\ngemma-3-1b-it decode step, median of 3 alternating rounds, RTX 3090:\n\n```\npython -m sglang.benchmark.one_batch --batch-size 1 8 32 --input-len 256 --output-len 128\n```\n\n| batch | main ms | this PR ms |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 5.65 | 4.94 |\n| 8 | 5.88 | 5.27 |\n| 32 | 6.75 | 6.13 |\n\ngemma-3-4b-it serving, random 128 in and 128 out, median TPOT over 2 runs per arm: 12.70 to 11.85 ms at concurrency 1, 12.88 to 12.08 ms at 8. The q and k norm pair goes from 20 kernels to 4 per layer.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41801824543](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801824543)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41801824649](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801824649)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41801824447](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801824447)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
